; The whole development: Lib (semantic domain), Lang (Verilog syntax, LFP semantics,
; ITree module layer, equivalence proof), Ex (RISC-V case study).
; `include_subdirs qualified` makes dune pick up .v files from the subdirectories and
; qualify them by path (VerilogRocq.Lang.Semantics), matching the `-R` layout the
; sources were written for.
; FreeSim and Ordinal are dune theories under dep/; the rest are installed theories from
; the Nix dev shell. Dune binds load paths only for theories listed here.
; RiscVITree (and its stdpp) provide the bit-vector value type of Lang/Events.v.
(include_subdirs qualified)

(coq.theory
 (name VerilogRocq)
 (theories Stdlib FreeSim Ordinal coqutil ITree Paco ExtLib stdpp RiscVITree)
 ; Syntax.v's custom-entry Verilog grammar triggers hundreds of
 ; notation-incompatible-prefix warnings on Rocq 9.0 that bury everything else.
 ; The case study parses through that grammar and builds, so they are silenced.
 (flags (:standard -w -notation-incompatible-prefix)))
